> I don't exactly remember the differences between VT220 and VT240.

VT240 did ReGIS graphics.  VT220 did not.

ReGIS was introduced on the VT125 which added a graphics processor
to the VT100.  It worked in parallel with the character cell engine.
Two display engines with output overlaid on the same monitor at the
same time.  The VT240 integrated the engines so that there was only
one bit map instead of two.  On the bright side, that meant that
you could do sixel downline dumps of your rendered ReGIS screen,
a low cost alternative to RGL.

But it's been a lot of years.  My recollection may be suspect.

